          "explanation": "Russell decomposes the sentence into existence, uniqueness, and predication claims joined by logical AND. Since no King of France exists, the existence conjunct is false, making the entire compound claim false — without needing to treat 'the King of France' as a genuinely referring expression pointing to some strange non-existent object.",
